"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    raw = sys.stdin.read()\n    data = raw.split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n\n    n = int(data[0])\n    vals = data[1:n + 1]\n\n    seen = set()\n    res = []\n    for v in vals:\n        if v in seen:\n            label = \"seen\"\n        else:\n            label = \"new\"\n            seen.add(v)\n        res.append(label)\n\n    for r in res:\n        print(r)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"The program scans a list of values, checking each one against a set of values seen so far. A value already in the set prints \"seen\"; a value not yet in the set prints \"new\" and joins it.",
